# Patch: Rosenthal congestion loss as a Megatron router load-balancing type
# ==================================
# Problem: Megatron ships aux_loss / global_aux_loss (linear-in-load, Switch-style) and sinkhorn.
#   The Exp 3 arms need two more balancing types, "rosenthal" and "global_rosenthal", which price
#   relative expert load through a congestion cost family instead of the fixed linear form, at
#   micro-batch and global-batch level respectively. "hard" + "linear" + lambda=1 must reduce
#   exactly to switch_load_balancing_loss_func for every topk, so the congestion loss is a strict
#   generalization of the existing Switch arm rather than a parallel implementation of it.
#
# What this patch does:
#   - transformer_config.py: declares moe_rosenthal_variant, moe_rosenthal_cost,
#     moe_rosenthal_lambda and moe_rosenthal_log_grad_ratio (the last is unread until patch 0004,
#     declared here so that patch touches neither this file nor training.py). Extends the
#     moe_router_load_balancing_type docstring and the two moe_expert_capacity_factor allow-lists.
#     Validates rules 1-4 and 8 of the shared config contract whenever a rosenthal type is
#     selected, plus that at most one of the two is selected at a time; rule 7 sits outside that
#     guard because it constrains every OTHER balancing type. Rules 5 and 6 are RETIRED, not
#     renumbered -- 0017's construction made 'soft' correct at any reduce-group size, and the
#     numbers stay retired because they are pinned into test names elsewhere.
#   - arguments.py: adds the two names to --moe-router-load-balancing-type's choices. This is the
#     only hand-written argparse edit needed; every moe_rosenthal_* flag is auto-generated from the
#     TransformerConfig fields above by ArgumentGroupFactory.
#   - router.py: is_aux_loss_enabled() also matches the two new types. Without that the router
#     never computes scores_for_aux_loss and the run trains with NO balancing while the config says
#     otherwise, with no error. TopKRouter._apply_rosenthal_loss() is added beside
#     _apply_global_aux_loss and called from the same gate in routing().
#     reset_global_aux_loss_tracker() resets the three rosenthal_* attributes under their own
#     condition, separate from global_aux_loss's: a global_rosenthal-only run never allocates
#     global_tokens_per_expert, so reusing that condition would skip the reset every global batch.
#     TopKRouter.__init__ gains a comment only -- see it for why the accumulators are not buffers.
#   - finalize_model_grads.py: reset_model_temporary_tensors's string match also matches
#     "global_rosenthal". Missing this dispatch is the most expensive silent failure in the change:
#     no error, the loss just prices a stale running average.
#   This patch adds no math and no metric names of its own. Every formula lives in
#   moe_congestion_routing.losses.rosenthal, imported function-locally as patch 0001 already does.
#   rosenthal_loss and rosenthal_pressure_max reach the log through moe_track_names, which has been
#   data-driven since patch 0001.
#
# Where in the code:
#   File: megatron/core/transformer/transformer_config.py
#   Location: the moe_router_load_balancing_type docstring (~line 662); the field block after
#     moe_aux_loss_coeff (~line 776); the MoE validation block beside the existing
#     moe_expert_capacity_factor checks (~line 1483).
#
#   File: megatron/training/arguments.py
#   Function: _add_moe_args()
#   Location: the --moe-router-load-balancing-type choices list (~line 3136).
#
#   File: megatron/core/transformer/moe/router.py
#   Function: is_aux_loss_enabled() / _apply_rosenthal_loss() / reset_global_aux_loss_tracker() /
#     routing()
#   Location: the is_aux_loss_enabled() loop (~line 279); a new method beside
#     _apply_global_aux_loss (~line 425); the aux-loss block in routing(), immediately after the
#     _apply_global_aux_loss call (~line 665); the reset block appended to
#     reset_global_aux_loss_tracker() (~line 859).
#
#   File: megatron/core/distributed/finalize_model_grads.py
#   Function: reset_model_temporary_tensors()
#   Location: the "global_aux_loss" string match (~line 324).
#
# How to fix if this patch breaks on a future Megatron version:
#   Search for "global_aux_loss" in transformer_config.py, router.py and finalize_model_grads.py
#   and add the rosenthal equivalent beside each hit; extend --moe-router-load-balancing-type's
#   choices in arguments.py. Two of those hits are upstream helpers this patch RE-IMPLEMENTS
#   rather than calls, because _apply_rosenthal_loss fuses two collectives into one and neither
#   helper supports that: moe_utils.py's get_tokens_per_expert_and_token_count (its
#   with_padding_mask branch and its total_num_tokens line) and _apply_global_aux_loss's
#   accumulate-then-divide-by-ga_steps protocol. A bump that changes either moves
#   aux_loss/seq_aux_loss/global_aux_loss and leaves rosenthal on the old definition -- a different
#   N in the denominator of u, or a different averaging window -- with no error. Re-derive both
#   copies from the new upstream shape rather than renaming fields.
#
# Known limitations:
#   - The distributed path has never actually run distributed. Every verification of this patch ran
#     at DP = CP = TP = 1, where each reduce group has size one and the fused all-reduce is a no-op.
#     Before any multi-GPU run, watch sum_e u_glob: it reads E when the reduce group is right, and
#     E * (ranks the numerator covers) / (ranks the denominator assumes) when it is not.
#   - Semi-gradient staleness under global_rosenthal: within a grad-accumulation window the loss
#     prices against the running average of the micro-batches seen so far, exactly as
#     global_aux_loss already does. Both variants inherit it; it is not introduced here.
#   - Megatron's OWN global_aux_loss still accumulates its counts and its step counter in
#     register_buffer, which Float16Module casts to bf16. This patch deliberately does not fix
#     that, because it would change global_aux_loss's numerics for every arm using it. No arm in
#     docs/plan.md trains with global_aux_loss today; if one ever does, its f_e carries up to ~1%
#     quantization at 256 grad-accumulation steps and its ga_steps saturates at 256.0, past which
#     the divisor freezes while the numerator keeps growing.
#   - This patch's routing() hunk does not carry patch 0001's added lines as context, even though
#     it lands two lines above them: _apply_expert_bias sits between the two insertion points in
#     the original file, widening the gap past the three lines git apply matches on. Confirmed by
#     grep, not predicted from line numbers. So 0001 may be amended without regenerating this one.
#
# Applied to: Megatron-LM core_v0.18.0
#
diff --git a/megatron/core/transformer/transformer_config.py b/megatron/core/transformer/transformer_config.py
